INT. ORBITAL HOSTEL - GALLEY - NIGHT CYCLE

A narrow galley under dim amber light. A foldable table. Pouches of food clipped to a rail. Through a porthole, the slow curve of a blue planet.

A WOMAN (30s, grey coverall, wrist tattoo) sits alone at the table, peeling the foil off a ration tray. She eats a small bite, looks at the porthole, eats another.

CASS (30s, medic jacket, bleary) floats in and anchors himself to a rail with his foot.

CASS
You're up.

WOMAN
You're up.

CASS
I couldn't sleep.

WOMAN
Me neither.

He fills a squeeze bulb at the dispenser, drinks, wipes his mouth. Looks at her tray.

CASS
Is that the chicken?

WOMAN
Allegedly.

HOWARD (60s, station steward, clipboard, a bad hip) enters, slow. He sees the Woman, stops.

HOWARD
Dr. Devi. I didn't know you'd come down.

DEVI
Neither did I, Howard.

He nods, studies her, glances at Cass. Cass takes another sip. Howard consults his clipboard.

HOWARD
The log says you're in quarantine.

DEVI
The log is early.

HOWARD
I'll note it.

DEVI
Note whatever you like.

Howard hesitates, then marks a line and shuffles out. Cass and Devi sit in the quiet. The planet turns outside.

CASS
You told them you were fine?

DEVI
I told them I was awake.
